"hadiths[16]{hadithnumber,text}:"
1097,"Narrated `Aisha:\n\nThe Prophet (ﷺ) said, \Bilal pronounces the Adhan at night ""1098"",Narrated `Abdullah bin `Umar:\n\nThe Prophet (ﷺ) cutoff the hand of a thief for stealing a shield that was worth three Dirhams."""
1098,"[AI-translation] Abdullah bin Umar said: The Prophet (peace be upon him) cut off the hand of a thief for a shield whose price was three dirhams.""
1099"""
1099,"Narrated Abu Huraira: The Prophet (ﷺ) said, ""Allah curses a thief who steals an egg and thus his hand is cut off, and who steals a rope and thus his hand is cut off."""
1100,"The people of Quraish worried about the lady from Bani Makhzum who had committed theft. They asked, Who will intercede for her with Allah's Messenger (ﷺ)?"" Some said"""
1101,"Abu Huraira reported that Sulaiman b. Dawud said:I will certainly have intercourse with seventy wives during the night, and every wife amongst them will give birth to a child, who will fight in the cause of Allah. It was said to him: Say: Insha' Allah"" (God willing)"""
1102,"A man came to Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) while he was in the mosque, and he called him, saying, ""O Allah's Apostle! I have committed illegal sexual intercourse.'"" The Prophet (ﷺ) turned his face to the other side, but that man repeated his statement four times, and after he bore witness against himself four times, the Prophet (ﷺ) called him, saying, ""Are you mad?"" The man said, ""No."" The Prophet (ﷺ) said, ""Are you married?"" The man said, ""Yes."" Then the Prophet (ﷺ) said, 'Take him away and stone him to death."" Jabir bin `Abdullah said: I was among the ones who participated in stoning him and we stoned him at the Musalla. When the stones troubled him, he fled, but we over took him at Al-Harra and stoned him to death."""
1103,"A man came to the Prophet (ﷺ) and said, I beseech you to judge us according to Allah's Laws."" Then his opponent who was wiser than he ""1104"",A'isha (Allah be pleased with her) reported that Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) bought from a Jew grain for a specified time; and gave him iron coat-of-mail of his as a pledge"""
1104,"[AI-translation] Abdullah bin Umar reported that the Jews came to the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) and mentioned to him that a man and a woman from among them had committed adultery. The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said to them: ""What do you find in the Torah concerning stoning?"" They said: ""We disgrace them and they are flogged."" Abdullah bin Salam said: ""You lie! It contains stoning."" So they brought the Torah and spread it open, and one of them placed his hand over the verse of stoning, and read what was before it and what was after it. Abdullah bin Salam said to him: ""Lift your hand."" So he lifted his hand, and there was the verse of stoning. They said: ""He has spoken the truth, O Muhammad, it contains the verse of stoning."" The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) ordered them, and they were stoned. Abdullah bin Umar said: I saw the man leaning over the woman, shielding her from the stones.""
1105"""
1105,"Narrated Ash-Shaibani: I asked 'Abdullah bin Abi Awfa, ""Did the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) stone (the adulterer)?"" He said, ""Yes."" I asked, ""Was it before Surat An-Nur was revealed or after it?"" He said, ""I do not know."""
1106,"The Prophet (ﷺ) said, If a lady slave commits illegal sexual intercourse and she is proved guilty of illegal sexual intercourse"""
1107,"Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) was asked regarding ghee (cooking butter) in which a mouse had fallen. He said, Take out the mouse and throw away the ghee around it and use the rest."""""""""
1108,"An Ansari woman asked the Prophet (ﷺ) how to take a bath after finishing from the menses. He replied, ""Take a piece a cloth perfumed with musk and clean the private parts with it thrice."" The Prophet (ﷺ) felt shy and turned his face. So I pulled her to me and told her what the Prophet (ﷺ) meant."""
1109,"One day Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) came out (before the people) and `Abdullah bin Hudhafa stood up and asked (him) ""Who is my father?"" The Prophet (ﷺ) replied, ""Your father is Hudhafa."" The Prophet (ﷺ) told them repeatedly (in anger) to ask him anything they liked. `Umar knelt down before the Prophet (ﷺ) and said thrice, ""We accept Allah as (our) Lord and Islam as (our) religion and Muhammad as (our) Prophet."" After that the Prophet (ﷺ) became silent."""
1110,"Anas reported that Allah's Messenger (may peace he upon him) wed to make this supplication:\\"" O Allah"""""""
1111,"who took part in the battle of Badr and was a Naqib (a person heading a group of six persons), on the night of Al-'Aqaba pledge: Allah's Apostle said while a group of his companions were around him, Swear allegiance to me for: 1. Not to join anything in worship along with Allah. 2. Not to steal. 3. Not to commit illegal sexual intercourse. 4. Not to kill your children. 5. Not to accuse an innocent person (to spread such an accusation among people). 6. Not to be disobedient (when ordered) to do good deed."" The Prophet (ﷺ) added: ""Whoever among you fulfills his pledge will be rewarded by Allah. And whoever indulges in any one of them (except the ascription of partners to Allah) and gets the punishment in this world"""
1112,"Abu Huraira said, ""Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) said, 'No one should prevent his neighbor from fixing a wooden peg in his wall."" Abu Huraira said (to his companions), ""Why do I find you averse to it? By Allah, I certainly will narrate it to you."""""""
